<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mariandynians</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mariandyni</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mariandynians were an Anatolian people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bithynia">Bithynia</a> and Paphlagonia, around Heraclea Pontica. After Greek colonists from Megara founded Heraclea in the 6th century BCE, many of them were reduced to a dependent rural population working the land, compared by ancient writers to the helots of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>.</p></div>
